{
  "description": "The airtime budget, draft 0 (draft/airtime.md). Shares are in millionths of a node's time and windows in seconds; a bucket fills at its share and holds its window of that, or one 255-byte frame if that is more, and is full at time 0. In parts, most_ppm is everything a node of that role may spend, routing at its largest, and relayed_ppm is null for a node that passes nothing on. In classes, part is the part of the budget that pays for a frame with that hdr, the node's own or passed on; flood_allowance names the bucket of draft/flooding.md that pays for it too; unpaid is what becomes of it when they do not all hold its airtime: it waits, it is dropped, or it is sent and charged, the bucket going no lower than empty; null where Routes' cap decides. In spends, a node of that role on that profile, every bucket full at time 0, is offered each frame in order at at_ns; airtime_ns is its time on the air (vectors/phy.json), and sent says whether it goes then; a frame that goes is charged to every bucket that pays for it, and one that does not to none. In estimates, the frames spent go as in spends, and at at_ns the node's own frames waiting go in the order given; wait_s is how many seconds, rounded up, until it goes: when every bucket that pays for it holds its airtime, and not before the frame ahead of it, each frame charged to its buckets as it goes. In reasons, a message of the node's own waits with or without a route and a session, and for the region's limit and the budget as long as given, in seconds; reason and wait are what the companion protocol shows.",
